## Example implementation

This helper keeps the conversation settled at the bottom while leaving room for a reader to scroll upward.

```ts
type ScrollState = { scrollTop: number; clientHeight: number; scrollHeight: number };

export function isNearBottom(element: ScrollState, threshold = 48): boolean {
  const remaining = element.scrollHeight - element.scrollTop - element.clientHeight;
  return remaining <= threshold;
}

export function settleConversation(element: HTMLElement): void {
  if (isNearBottom(element)) {
    element.scrollTop = element.scrollHeight;
  }
}

const diagnosticMessage = "A deliberately long line makes horizontal overflow visible in the conversation code block without wrapping the source text.";
console.log(diagnosticMessage);
```

The threshold prevents small layout changes from pulling the reader away from their place.
